###Text
Text test::opalwillow2::text::BinderyNotes
{
  type: markdown;
  content: '# Conservation Bindery Register\n\nThis model publishes the register of a book-conservation bindery as a domain contract.\nFifteen classes carry typed scalar properties, optional properties and to-many label\ncollections, and seven bidirectional associations wire them into one navigable graph.\n\n## Navigable chains\n\n* A workshop reaches its benches, a bench its conservators, a conservator the treatment\n  rounds it leads, a round the volume it was booked against and the condition reports\n  written on it - five associations chained through shared end classes, so navigation from\n  a workshop reaches a condition report in five hops and back again from either end.\n* A volume reaches the text blocks bound into it and a text block its folded gatherings,\n  a second chain that meets the first at the volume end.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nNo store, mapping, connection or runtime is declared: the classes are published purely as\na contract, so the EMIT run exercises parse and compile of the class graph, the diagram\nview laid out over it and this documentation element. Reader-ticket administration,\nexhibition gallery layouts and the materials store inventory are not reachable from here.\n';
}
